<title>MEXICO: Mexico's vehicle production up in Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexico's vehicle production up in Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's automobile industry produced 306,544 vehicles during the first three months of the year versus 301,143 units produced during the same period in 1996, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association (AMIA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Mexico also exported 229,010 units during the year's first quarter, down from 240,315 during the year-ago period.  </p>
<p>The AMIA report said the decline in export sales reflects a 7.4 percent drop in demand from the United States and Canada, where sales fell down to 204,092 units for the time period.</p>
<p>Sales to Central America rose 54 percent to 3,050 units, sales to South America rose 8.8 percent to 20,087 units and sales to the Far East declined 66.7 percent to 571 units, the report said.</p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods.  </p>
<p>				   JAN-MARCH 97	    JAN-MARCH 96</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	     306,544		  301,143</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	  72,843		   53,296</p>
<p>		autos		   52,022		   34,506</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    20,821		   18,790</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   233,701		  247,847</p>
<p>		autos		  137,800		  167,974</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    95,901		   79,873</p>
<p>    TOTAL SALES		    323,354		  311,358</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	  94,344		   71,043</p>
<p>		autos		   58,873		   41,807</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    35,471		   29,236</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   299,010		  240,315</p>
<p>		autos		  133,044		  161,032</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    95,966		   79,283</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES  89,386		   67,849</p>
<p>		autos		   55,857		   42,616</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    33,529		   25,233</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
